{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '35,82p' src/cljc/dao/data/btree/storage.cljc; sed -n '1025,1065p' src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc; sed -n '475,500p' docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md; rg -n 'overshoot|deadline|tick' src/cljc/yin/vm/ffi/remote_channel.cljc | head -12; cat deps.edn | head -90\"","aggregated_output":"(def ^:private absent\n  \"Identity sentinel for handle misses (§5.1 sketch): keywords are not\n   reliably `identical?` on cljs, an opaque host object is.\"\n  #?(:cljd (Object.)\n     :clj (Object.)\n     :cljs (js-obj)))\n\n\n(deftype KVStorage\n  [store settings verify? algorithm]\n\n  bt/IStorage\n\n  (-store\n    [_ node]\n    (let [blob (bt/node->blob node)]\n      (if algorithm\n        (jing/materialize! store blob {:algorithm algorithm})\n        (jing/materialize! store blob))))\n\n\n  (-restore\n    [_ addr]\n    (let [blob (jing/get store addr absent)]\n      (when (identical? blob absent)\n        (throw (ex-info \"missing index segment\" {:address addr})))\n      (when verify?\n        (when-not (jing/segment-matches? addr blob)\n          (throw (ex-info \"corrupt index segment\"\n                          {:expected addr, :actual (jing/segment-key blob)}))))\n      (bt/blob->node blob settings)))\n\n\n  (-accessed [_ _addr] nil)\n\n\n  (-settings [_] settings))\n\n\n(defn kv-storage\n  \"A sync IStorage over a dao.jing content-store handle. opts:\n   {:branching-factor n (default 512) :ref-type k (default per host, §5.3)\n   :verify? bool (default false, §5.2 — same-host mint+read only)\n   :algorithm keyword (default nil, mints with default-hash-algorithm)}. The\n   returned storage owns the Settings every tree restored through it shares\n   (§5.1 threading rule); pass the manifest's :branching-factor here.\"\n  ([store] (kv-storage store nil))\n  ([store opts]\n  [binding {:keys [fixed rest], :as parsed} tuple]\n  (when (tuple-shape-matches? parsed tuple)\n    (let [b (reduce (fn [b [term value]]\n                      (or (unify b term value) (reduced nil)))\n                    binding\n                    (map vector fixed tuple))]\n      (when b\n        (if (and rest (not= rest '_))\n          (unify b rest (subvec (vec tuple) (count fixed)))\n          b)))))\n\n\n(defn- and-then\n  [x f]\n  (when (some? x) (f x)))\n\n\n(defn- select-datoms\n  [idx e a v]\n  (select-by-index idx e a v))\n\n\n(defn- db-sym?\n  [x]\n  (and (symbol? x) (= \\$ (first (name x)))))\n\n\n(defn- classify-in-pattern\n  [pattern]\n  (cond (db-sym? pattern) :db\n        (symbol? pattern) :scalar\n        (and (vector? pattern) (vector? (first pattern))) :relation\n        (and (vector? pattern) (= '... (last pattern))) :coll\n        (vector? pattern) :tuple\n        :else (throw (ex-info \"Unknown :in pattern\" {:pattern pattern}))))\n\n\n(defn- expand-in-binding\n  [pattern value dbs]\n  (case (classify-in-pattern pattern)\n    :db [{::dbs {pattern (get dbs pattern)}}]\n- **Finite admission cap (`:max-sessions`)**: An accepting channel composition\n  enforces an upper bound on active concurrent sessions. When `:max-sessions`\n  is reached, newcomer offers are cleanly rejected (their offered socket\n  handles closed and accept acknowledgements withheld) after reaping expired\n  and closed sessions.\n- **Idle reaping (`:idle-timeout`)**: `:idle-timeout` is a positive integer\n  in milliseconds, measured against the driver-supplied `now`; its alias\n  `:idle-timeout-ms` takes precedence when both are given. Sessions with no\n  progress or activity for at least `:idle-timeout` milliseconds are reaped\n  on accept-step ticks; their underlying socket handles and channel rings\n  are closed to release resources and restore capacity.\n- **Step event budget (`budget`)**: Channel projection `step!` loops accept an\n  optional event budget. When specified, at most `budget` events are read and\n  processed from the traffic medium per tick, preventing continuous traffic\n  floods from starving other processing or hanging driver ticks. An\n  accepting composition takes it as `:step-budget`, applied to each\n  session's projection on every accept-step tick. Beside it the accepting\n  composition takes `:mirror-budget` and `:chase-budget` (each a positive\n  integer or nil), passed to each session's `mirror-step` as its `bounds`\n  (2.3). A dialing composition takes the same three keys for its\n  `dial-step!` projection and mirror.\n- **Link bounds**: the asking side's link takes\n  `:dao.stream.remote/drain-budget`, `:dao.stream.remote/max-outstanding`\n  and `:dao.stream.remote/max-filed` (2.4), bounding the reads per drain,\n  the requests in flight or kept, and the answers and prefetched outcomes\n  retained per link. A dialing composition passes them to its link with the\nrg: src/cljc/yin/vm/ffi/remote_channel.cljc: IO error for operation on src/cljc/yin/vm/ffi/remote_channel.cljc: No such file or directory (os error 2)\n{:deps {org.clojure/core.async {:mvn/version \"1.8.741\"}\n        org.clojure/tools.reader {:mvn/version \"1.5.0\"}\n        ring/ring {:mvn/version \"1.14.1\"}\n        com.cognitect/transit-clj {:mvn/version \"1.0.333\"}\n        org.replikativ/boring {:mvn/version \"0.1.30\"}\n        com.datomic/peer {:mvn/version \"1.0.7364\"}\n        org.postgresql/postgresql {:mvn/version \"42.7.3\"}\n        org.clojure/data.json {:mvn/version \"2.5.0\"}\n        http-kit/http-kit {:mvn/version \"2.8.0\"}\n        org.jsoup/jsoup {:mvn/version \"1.18.3\"}\n        instaparse/instaparse {:mvn/version \"1.5.0\"}\n        ;; yang.python.antlr: the runtime the generated Python3 parser runs\n        ;; on; pinned to the tool version in :antlr-gen (they are one release)\n        org.antlr/antlr4-runtime {:mvn/version \"4.13.2\"}\n        criterium/criterium {:mvn/version \"0.4.6\"}\n        io.github.rctcwyvrn/blake3 {:mvn/version \"1.3\"}\n        stigmergy/chp {:mvn/version \"0.1.0-SNAPSHOT\"\n                       :exclusions [refactor-nrepl/refactor-nrepl]}}\n :cljd/opts {}\n ;; build/antlr/python3/classes: the generated Python3 parser, produced by\n ;; `clj -M:antlr-gen` (antlr/python3/manifest.edn); absent until generated\n :paths [\"src/clj\" \"src/cljc\" \"src/cljs\" \"src/cljd\"\n         \"build/antlr/python3/classes\"]\n :aliases {:clean {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                   :exec-fn clean/clean}\n           :profile-btree {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                           :extra-deps {persistent-sorted-set/persistent-sorted-set\n                                        {:mvn/version \"0.3.0\"}}\n                           :main-opts [\"-m\" \"btree-bench\"]}\n           :test {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                  :extra-deps {io.github.cognitect-labs/test-runner\n                               {:git/tag \"v0.5.1\" :git/sha \"dfb30dd\"}}\n                  :main-opts [\"-m\" \"cognitect.test-runner\"]\n                  :exec-fn cognitect.test-runner.api/test}\n           :nREPL {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                   :extra-deps {nrepl/nrepl {:mvn/version \"1.0.0\"}\n                                cider/cider-nrepl {:mvn/version \"0.58.0\"}}\n                   :main-opts [\"-m\" \"nrepl.cmdline\" \"--middleware\" \"[cider.nrepl/cider-middleware]\"]}\n           :cljs {:extra-paths [\"test\" \"src/dev\" \"build/antlr/python3/js\"]\n                  :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \"3.3.5\"}\n                               reagent/reagent {:mvn/version \"2.0.1\"}\n                               com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \"0.8.280\"}}}\n           :dev {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                 :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \"3.3.5\"}\n                              cider/cider-nrepl {:mvn/version \"0.58.0\"}\n                              reagent/reagent {:mvn/version \"2.0.1\"}\n                              com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \"0.8.280\"}\n                              ;; benchmark baseline + psset-fixtures\n                              ;; generator only; production uses\n                              ;; dao.data.btree\n                              persistent-sorted-set/persistent-sorted-set\n                              {:mvn/version \"0.3.0\"}}\n                 :jvm-opts [\"-Dconfig=config.clj\"]}\n           ;; The one ClojureDart pin. Compose it with the build aliases:\n           ;; clj -M:clojuredart:cljd ..., clj -M:clojuredart:cljd-yin-repl-build ...\n           :clojuredart {:extra-deps {sonwh98/clojuredart\n                                      {:git/url \"https://github.com/sonwh98/ClojureDart.git\"\n                                       :sha \"7d00ee2aa7fa9d990581e78ebc4a66b93cb70a31\"}\n                                      }}\n           :cljd {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                  :main-opts [\"-m\" \"cljd.build\"]\n                  :cljd/opts {:kind :flutter :main datomworld.demo.main}}\n           :server {:extra-deps {http-kit/http-kit {:mvn/version \"2.8.0\"}}\n                    :jvm-opts [\"-Dconfig=config.clj\"]\n                    :main-opts [\"-m\" \"world.server\"]}\n           :clj-yin-repl {:main-opts [\"-m\" \"yin.repl.main\"]}\n           ;; jolt host configuration (docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md\n           ;; §4.2-4.3), run through build/tools/jolt/bin/jolt -Srepro -M:jolt.\n           ;; src/jolt precedes src/cljc so a host override wins; src/clj is\n           ;; listed for audited portable namespaces only (its JVM namespaces\n           ;; are selected away by :jolt reader branches, never loaded). No\n           ;; generated Java parser classes, no JS/Dart roots, and no\n           ;; dependency coordinate is fetched until a jolt-loaded namespace\n           ;; needs one.\n           :jolt {:replace-paths [\"src/jolt\" \"src/cljc\" \"src/clj\"]\n                  :replace-deps {}}\n           :jolt-yin-repl {:main-opts [\"-m\" \"yin.repl.main\"]}\n           ;; composed after :jolt (-M:jolt:jolt-test): the oracle tests and\n           ;; src/dev (src/dev/jolt_test_runner.clj and its sentinel)\n           :jolt-test {:extra-paths [\"test\" \"src/dev\"]}\n           ;; DIAGNOSTIC only (-M:jolt:jolt-diag:jolt-test): a jolt stand-in\n           ;; for the corpus loader dao.jing.cbor-fixtures, whose root must\n           ;; precede test (src/dev/jolt_diag/dao/jing/cbor_fixtures.cljc);\n           ;; jolt puts :extra-paths roots first, in alias order (-Spath)\n           :jolt-diag {:extra-paths [\"src/dev/jolt_diag\"]}\n           :cljs-yin-repl\n           {:extra-paths [\"test\" \"src/dev\"]\n            :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \"3.3.5\"}\n                         reagent/reagent {:mvn/version \"2.0.1\"}\n                         com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \"0.8.280\"}}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"agent_message","text":"Mode 1 puts more weight on view projection, pagination, and bounded execution than on advanced rules. I’ll keep the phase IDs but schedule timeout work before aggregate and rule expansion. One detail needs strengthening: checks around a range scan alone cannot guarantee “within one storage read,” because a lazy scan may fetch several nodes. The spec will require checks around each actual node fetch and account for work that produces no binding."}}
